<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers sold steady to $1.00 per cwt higher, compared to Monday, USDA said. Demand was good. Good attendance farmer feeder buyers. 82 percent over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Steers: Medium and Large 1: 500-500 lbs 87.00-92.00; 550-600 lbs 85.50, some thin and or Blk-Blkwf 93.75; 600-700 lbs 82.25-86.75, some fleshy 73.50; 700-800 lbs 73.75-77.75, some fleshy 74.00; 800-900 lbs 71.50-75.25, some Blk-Blkwf to 77.00; 900-1000 lbs 69.90-74.30, some Blk-Blkwf 75.50; 1000-1050 lbs 69.50, some Limo X 70.40; 1050-1100 lbs 70.40.</p>
<p>Heifers: Medium and Large 1: 500-600 lbs 72.00-78.00, some Blk-Blkwf 84.50; 600-700 lbs 72.00-75.70, some thin 78.00; 700-800 lbs 69.90-73.10; 800-900 lbs 67.50-69.70; 900-1000 lbs 64.00-66.00. Receipts: This Week 2,139  Last Week 2,411  Last Year 2,811</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
